WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.047 --> 00:00:03.055
(bell ringing)

00:00:03.055 --> 00:00:05.805
(cheerful music)

00:00:07.332 --> 00:00:08.445
- [Voiceover] How many times do you get

00:00:08.445 --> 00:00:10.099
one of the only people in the
world doing what you're doing?

00:00:10.099 --> 00:00:12.251
There's other people that tried it,

00:00:12.251 --> 00:00:14.339
but they haven't lasted.

00:00:14.339 --> 00:00:16.283
- My name's Art Ritchie and I'm one of

00:00:16.283 --> 00:00:18.147
the co-owners of the Carousel Works.

00:00:18.147 --> 00:00:20.579
- And I'm Dan Jones,
and I'm the other owner

00:00:20.579 --> 00:00:22.079
of Carousel Works.

00:00:23.848 --> 00:00:25.096
- [Art] We're the largest manufacturer

00:00:25.096 --> 00:00:27.846
of wooden carousels in the world.

00:00:30.951 --> 00:00:35.118
- Art and I met through a
third party that we both knew.

00:00:37.167 --> 00:00:38.647
I went over to his shop one day,

00:00:38.647 --> 00:00:41.471
and we were talking and
one thing led to another,

00:00:41.471 --> 00:00:43.490
and from there it just kinda took off.

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:45.991
I was doing restoration
and he was doing carvings.

00:00:45.991 --> 00:00:48.815
- We've had a 50/50
partnership for 30 years,

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:50.321
and there are very few partnerships

00:00:50.321 --> 00:00:53.239
that last over three years, so.

00:00:53.239 --> 00:00:54.543
- You know that's not
to say that we haven't

00:00:54.543 --> 00:00:57.359
had differences over the years.

00:00:57.359 --> 00:00:59.618
It's just like being married.

00:00:59.618 --> 00:01:00.466
But not that bad.

00:01:00.466 --> 00:01:02.716
(laughter)

00:01:05.271 --> 00:01:07.817
- [Art] We average, in different stages,

00:01:07.817 --> 00:01:09.991
probably three carousels a year.

00:01:09.991 --> 00:01:12.881
- [Dan] We're actually
working on four right now.

00:01:12.881 --> 00:01:15.015
We have carousels all around the world.

00:01:15.015 --> 00:01:17.151
- [Art] We made the Cincinnati
Riverfront carousel.

00:01:17.151 --> 00:01:18.762
- [Dan] We have one in the Bronx Zoo.

00:01:18.762 --> 00:01:20.176
- [Art] We have one in
the Kansas City Zoo.

00:01:20.176 --> 00:01:21.383
- [Dan] the Nashville Zoo.

00:01:21.383 --> 00:01:22.487
- [Art] the Atlanta Zoo.

00:01:22.487 --> 00:01:23.611
- [Dan] the Riverbank Zoo.

00:01:23.611 --> 00:01:27.091
- We even made the Smithsonian
National Zoo carousel.

00:01:27.091 --> 00:01:29.311
Carousels will put people
in the eye of the child.

00:01:29.311 --> 00:01:31.682
- Oh, they're absolutely beautiful.

00:01:31.682 --> 00:01:34.644
When you watch people ride a carousel,

00:01:34.644 --> 00:01:37.113
the kids are just loving
to go up and down,

00:01:37.113 --> 00:01:39.169
and with these big smiles.

00:01:39.169 --> 00:01:40.346
And then the ride comes to a stop.

00:01:40.346 --> 00:01:41.679
Can we go again?

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:43.819
It's fantastic.

